- Summary:: This article explores a model of learning that highlights the effectiveness of various learning strategies at different stages of the learning process. It identifies over 400 strategies that help learners plan, monitor, and evaluate their progress. The study suggests that the best learning strategies depend on the student's awareness of success criteria and the specific phase of learning they are in.
